`using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` is already imported in this file.

### 4. ArmEnvironment.cs (IL2026, IL3050)
File: `/tmp/sv-da84990db6c1493e8fb44162e3e0e04a/before/ArmEnvironment.cs`

Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Replace with manual JSON construction. The struct has `Endpoint` (Uri), `Audience` (string), and `DefaultScope` (string) properties:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\",\"DefaultScope\":\"{DefaultScope}\"}}";
}
```

Or better, use `Utf8JsonWriter`:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    var buffer = new System.Buffers.ArrayBufferWriter<byte>();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(buffer))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint?.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteString("DefaultScope", DefaultScope);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(buffer.WrittenSpan);
}
```

Add `using System.Buffers;` if needed. `System.Text.Json` is already imported.

